All in his mind?

A phenomenal and haunting psychological thriller about loneliness, social inequalities and mental illness. Portrays a true reflection of society; Dark, heartless and unforgiving. Jiiva puts in a horrifying performance as a sociopath and he absolutely nails it. Each passing minute, Prabhakar becomes more and more irredeemable but you can't help but sympathize with him. Ram intricately weaves in numerous Thiruvalluvar quotes and themes like, "without dignity, there is no man," which plays a big role in the characterization of Prabhakar. Right up until the end, Ram keeps the audience guessing as you never know what will happen to Prabhakar next. That mystery is what elevates the film even further and it ends with an incredibly powerful and important scene; Did it really even happen?

Stunning direction, beautiful cinematography and A+ acting. Tamil cinema at its finest.
